	<section class="rc-depends dh-section" style="margin-top: var(--section)" aria-labelledby="h-depends">
		<div class="dh-wrap">
			<div class="dh-stack" style="gap:24px">
				<p class="dh-kicker">More than a gut feeling</p>
				<h2 class="rc-quote" id="h-depends" data-quote>“<s>It depends.</s>”<span class="then">On what, exactly?</span></h2>
				<p class="dh-lead">Whether a joke connects or hurts does not depend on its words alone. The intention, the way the punchline is built, the perspective of the person telling it, possible differences in power and the situation all play a part.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="rc-factors">
				<div class="rc-factor dh-rise"><span class="ic" style="--c: var(--peach)"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#0b303b" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5h16v11H9l-5 4z"/><path d="M8 9h8M8 12h5"/></svg></span><h3>Topic &amp; punchline</h3><p>What are we laughing at, and how? Some topics are particularly sensitive. At the same time, it makes a difference whether a punchline relies on clichés, exaggerates in a surprising way or mainly belittles.</p><p class="q">“What are we actually laughing at here, and why?”</p></div>
				<div class="rc-factor dh-rise"><span class="ic" style="--c: var(--lime)"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#0b303b" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r=".8" fill="#0b303b"/></svg></span><h3>Intention &amp; function</h3><p>Is someone trying to connect, provoke, criticise or put others down? A statement delivered ironically need not reflect the actual attitude of the person telling it.</p><p class="q">“What is this joke meant to achieve?”</p></div>
				<div class="rc-factor dh-rise"><span class="ic" style="--c: var(--peach)"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#0b303b" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 12s3.5-6 9-6 9 6 9 6-3.5 6-9 6-9-6-9-6z"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2.5"/></svg></span><h3>Perspective &amp; target group</h3><p>Who is making fun of whom? It can make a difference whether someone jokes about their own group or speaks about others from an outside perspective.</p><p class="q">“Who is the butt of the punchline?”</p></div>
				<div class="rc-factor dh-rise"><span class="ic" style="--c: var(--lime)"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#0b303b" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="8" cy="9" r="3"/><circle cx="16" cy="9" r="3"/><path d="M3 19c.8-3 2.8-4.5 5-4.5s4.2 1.5 5 4.5M11 19c.8-3 2.8-4.5 5-4.5s4.2 1.5 5 4.5"/></svg></span><h3>Power relations</h3><p>Who has more status, influence or reach in this situation? And can the people at whose expense the joke may be made answer back?</p><p class="q">“Who has the stage here, and who can make themselves heard?”</p></div>
				<div class="rc-factor dh-rise"><span class="ic" style="--c: var(--peach)"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#0b303b" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8"/><path d="M12 8v4l3 2"/></svg></span><h3>Context</h3><p>A joke in a comedy club can land differently from the same joke in a classroom or at a funeral. Expectations, timing and the make-up of the audience shape its possible effect.</p><p class="q">“Does this humour suit this moment and this audience?”</p></div>
				<div class="rc-factor rc-factor--sum dh-rise"><p>The Humour Risk Check helps you look at these factors one by one and better judge how they interact.</p><p class="big">That turns a vague “it depends” into a reasoned assessment.</p></div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="dh-section dh-wrap" id="so-gehts" aria-labelledby="h-so">
		<p class="dh-kicker dh-rise">How it works</p>
		<h2 class="dh-h2 dh-rise" id="h-so" style="margin-top:16px">Three steps to your assessment</h2>
		<ol class="rc-steps">
			<li class="dh-rise"><b>Picture the joke and the situation</b><span>Think of a specific joke, a comedy clip or a humorous remark. Who says what, to whom and in what situation?</span></li>
			<li class="dh-rise"><b>Choose your check</b><span>The Quick Check lets you rate five key factors directly. The Deep Dive goes into more detail with 15 statements. You do not need any scientific background.</span></li>
			<li class="dh-rise"><b>Understand your results</b><span>You get a structured assessment of the potential risk of causing hurt and can see which factors carry particular weight. What you do with it is up to you.</span></li>
		</ol>

		<div class="rc-tool" id="check">
			<span class="dh-status" style="background: var(--lime)"><i></i>Science-based prototype</span>
			<h2 class="dh-h2" style="font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 38px)">The Humour Risk Check starts here</h2>
			<p class="dh-lead" style="max-width: 60ch">Humour can connect, provoke and sometimes hurt. This check helps you gauge how much potential a joke has to hurt others, and which factors play a part.</p>
			<p>Choose between a quick assessment and a more in-depth analysis.</p>
			<div class="rc-modes"><span><b>Quick Check</b> 5 factors</span><span><b>Deep Dive</b> 15 statements</span></div>
<!-- /wp:html -->
